    "Keys: reader (da-guard: ParseDomainPolicies; tenant-api: parseConfig),",
    "then the corpus row `id`. Value: \"unusable\" (the reader refuses the file,",
    "or da-guard reports a Problem that fails its run), else the policies it",
    "reads, in the corpus's verdict shape. A row absent here reads as PyYAML",
    "reads it — \"unusable\" when the generator blocks on it under --validate",
    "--strict (the row's `pyyaml_strict_blocks`). A tenant-api refusal of a",
    "row PyYAML reads is recorded \"unusable\" like any other difference (the",
    "catalog test ranks it go_refuses).",
    "Every entry must match one entry of reader_divergence_catalog.yaml,",
    "which tests/shared/test_reader_divergence_catalog.py checks, computing",
    "each row's direction."
